# LLM edits — token discipline

## Before changing
- Read only the relevant slice (offset/limit), not an entire 20–70 KB file.
- Find the symbol first (`Grep`) / API (`export function`), then read the surrounding code.
- Large files: `wizard.js`, `terrain.js`, `main.js`, `audio.js`, `volcano.js`, `critter.js`, `longneck.js`, `worm.js`, `comet.js`, `demon.js`.

## How to write
- **Do not** rewrite a whole file (`Write` on an existing .js) unless it is a new file or an explicit full rewrite request.
- Prefer surgical patches (StrReplace / small diff). One change = one area.
- Do not change formatting, imports, or naming outside the diff.
- Do not delete neighboring code “just in case” or add out-of-scope refactors.

## Response
- Do not paste entire files. At most a short diff / 5–15 lines of context.
- After a fix, do not dump the whole file “as it looks now”.
- Do not restate the task; briefly: what changed + where.

## Scope
- One mechanic / one bug = one mental PR. Do not mix spell + net + UI unless the user asks.
- Tuning constants → `js/config.js` / `js/spells/defs.js`, not scattered magic literals.
